{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794791543,"nonce":"hXmyDrulgr6OhJnf/qRUQEvLgF4=","title":"Enter and Space reach a focused div only as a click; the two cannot be told apart","message":"The window takes Tab, Enter and Space for navigation first (handle_navigation_key). Enter and Space become a click on the focused element and no KEY_DOWN follows, so a widget cannot distinguish Enter from Space. A widget that wants Space to pick up and Enter to open has no way to do it.\n\nEvidence: blinc_app windowed event loop input handling and the offscreen test helper that mirrors it; a key handler on a focused div never sees codes 13 or 32, only on_click with keyboard focus.\n\nExpected: a way for a focused element to receive the raw key (or the key code on the synthesised click).\n\nWorkaround in the caller: treat both as one Activate action.\n\nStand: waits for the Blinc team / fork; no change made here.","files":null}]}